{"title":"1970 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_November_2024)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, November 2024)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be integers greater than 1, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the bases of two number systems.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb9b7352942e18a3df49fadca0f6a49f3508209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d555a2fb62bf338fd13e9d9ced457fe49932324e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> are numbers in the system with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48bfec2c31c2b18baee6d1e13e5a9fd2c1e3c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610bb8d6a25ceeb883b9231cdd91040b0edd4b3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> are numbers in the system with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />; these are related as follows:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a586998d75a187fea58e7ee52af8bef2e60b6232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n} = x_{n}x_{n-1}\\cdots x_{0}, A_{n-1} = x_{n-1}x_{n-2}\\cdots x_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"340\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48bd19f678728b2bbd22b217426944ee6756746d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{n} = x_{n}x_{n-1}\\cdots x_{0}, B_{n-1} = x_{n-1}x_{n-2}\\cdots x_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"337\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6c1bf7c40be1b37fae76b48ff47d08a5ca765c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n} \\neq 0, x_{n-1} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Prove:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b328b6915b9e2b578357b032ee63063f261701c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A_{n-1}}{A_{n}} &lt; \\frac{B_{n-1}}{B_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8ed1fc54739081e1cc984b300a5b1bd0a984f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  Then for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8bd783106b994e36de8d06f48c60745a21f881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le k \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/561cbfb509b3a143c2dc8ae442983c90fd5d8f0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n x_k a^n b^k \\ge x_n x_k b^n a^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />, with equality only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce7f2c8cac20b2e92da94b9f7f38542e36c9973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=n$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e09a5367676e7425fee60f5945e1be1693b7080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.  (In particular, we have strict inequality for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0516fff77c0785613a80fac8278f140226dbf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />.)  In summation, this becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e06ff68cfdc98c46aee571a308657dacfd6b6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_n a^n \\sum_{k=0}^n x_k b^k &gt; x_n b^n \\sum_{k=0}^n x_k a^k,\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"48\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb366209ac46f8af4d0625f473eb9de13671741.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_n a^n \\cdot B_n &gt; x_n b^n \\cdot A_n,\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"16\" />\nwhich is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f0cc74c8a90648dd8ff9217293cc7db13b7f50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x_n a^n}{A_n} &gt; \\frac{x_n b^n}{B_n} .\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"40\" />\nThis implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e0e6b9a456db76559dc33bd80b9c4803b9dd5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{A_{n-1}}{A_n} = 1 - \\frac{x_n a^n}{A_n} &lt; 1 - \\frac{x_n b^n}{B_n} = \\frac{B_{n-1}}{B_n} .\\]\" width=\"306\" height=\"40\" />\nOn the other hand, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, then evidently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c70e719b5294ae7bea67741959244072e8619e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n-1}/A_n = B_{n-1}/B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then by what we have just shown, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/2600e9dc946054fc3c759b8a77b611a96f4b2b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n-1}/A_n &gt; B_{n-1}/B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />.  Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9a2e94987804246b75eaf0c6e1e1a040299f0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n-1}/A_n &lt; B_{n-1}/B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, as desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_November_2024.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_November_2024)\">Remarks (added by pf02, November 2024)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, November 2024)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>1. A comment about the problem: it is disappointing.  It is surprisingly\neasy compared to other problems given at an International Mathematical\nOlympiad, and frankly, uninteresting.\n</p><p>2. It is not stated with the usual rigor typical at this competition.  The\nproblem is really the following two statements:\n</p><p>S1: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/6349d82e9cb84b0d990c9ab058cd506650a4bdd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/044162d95d00589b6d420382b3f85245ecda0102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n, x_{n-1}, \\cdots, x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" /> be integers,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/660cf948694f7812bbe43b814f27d07cfce72442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k &lt; a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878b22b51cc3d9a8c2b555647cfef197c7c76eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/feefde5ce55247b282101af636fc4e9296640176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n-1}, \\cdots, x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> not all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nDefine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e44327b0841a3f5a7dce11fc9cdfbab2865192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n, A_{n-1}, B_n, B_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> as described in the problem.  If\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f715e56e85332da8fb18b5fac848466cc917972e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A_{n-1}}{A_{n}} &lt; \\frac{B_{n-1}}{B_{n}}\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"181\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8ed1fc54739081e1cc984b300a5b1bd0a984f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>S2: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8ed1fc54739081e1cc984b300a5b1bd0a984f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then (1) is true for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/044162d95d00589b6d420382b3f85245ecda0102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n, x_{n-1}, \\cdots, x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>3. I will give a variation of the solution in which the computations\nand argumentation are slightly simpler and more direct.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite inequality (1), and give a few steps in which we state\nequivalent inequalities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/781a596e9804ea346bed813b224aca0e4c6edd52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_{n-1} a^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 a + x_0}{x_n a^n + x_{n-1} a^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 a + x_0} &lt; \\frac{x_{n-1} b^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 b + x_0}{x_n b^n + x_{n-1} b^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 b + x_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"560\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba795b224c22dbc75802f534f25d1222edb86622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_{n-1} a^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 a + x_0}{x_n a^n} &lt; \\frac{x_{n-1} b^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 b + x_0}{x_n b^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"441\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdcf41b2ec752da6d37dadbd549e0f4680e85cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_{n-1} a^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 a + x_0}{a^n} &lt; \\frac{x_{n-1} b^{n-1} + \\cdots + x_1 b + x_0}{b^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"441\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64e42056291bf430c9f6e486a19dfe8a115aa58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n-1} \\frac{1}{a} + \\cdots + x_1 \\frac{1}{a^{n-1}} + x_0 \\frac{1}{a^n} &lt; x_{n-1} \\frac{1}{b} + \\cdots + x_1 \\frac{1}{b^{n-1}} + x_0 \\frac{1}{b^n}\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"561\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now it is clear that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8ed1fc54739081e1cc984b300a5b1bd0a984f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> then (2) is true for any\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/044162d95d00589b6d420382b3f85245ecda0102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n, x_{n-1}, \\cdots, x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />.  This proves statement S2 from the Remarks.\n</p><p>(Note that the problem said <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2db08f71f5160db64834deaf0bcd5451aa3c7e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n, x_{n-1} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.  This is not necessary.\nAll we need is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878b22b51cc3d9a8c2b555647cfef197c7c76eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed83518fc42087f5611b85784d67826ac4986470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n-1}, \\cdots, x_1, x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" />\nis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed78cc365b6ff8288eede1c01b2c1baa3cc2b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />.)\n</p><p>We prove statement S1 from the Remarks by contradiction.  We want to show\nthat if (1) is true for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab265ee383339b73fcf506ffaea8f49267c367b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n, \\cdots, x_1, x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8ed1fc54739081e1cc984b300a5b1bd0a984f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e1900f9ae83cebcbb5735f6c7bd6b6c505ba55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.  If we had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> then (1) would be an equality, not an\ninequality.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> then by S1, it would follow that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/d/88d0060a03b181d5ccda5d8cf7a6327d51c9a715.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A_{n-1}}{A_{n}} &gt; \\frac{B_{n-1}}{B_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"114\" height=\"42\" /> for all values of \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab265ee383339b73fcf506ffaea8f49267c367b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n, \\cdots, x_1, x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" /> which contradicts the hypothesis.  Either way, we\nget a contradiction, which proves S1.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, November 2024]\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1970_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>